          "message": {
            "text": "Projective activation is based on geometry, not on matrix3d syntax. The fourth-corner identity q2 = q1 + q3 - q0 separates affine planes that SVG can keep as vectors from genuinely projective quads; an authored perspective context also activates the boundary because its descendant flattening and depth composition cannot be represented by SVG groups.",
            "markdown": "Projective activation is based on geometry, not on matrix3d syntax. The fourth-corner identity q2 = q1 + q3 - q0 separates affine planes that SVG can keep as vectors from genuinely projective quads; an authored perspective context also activates the boundary because its descendant flattening and depth composition cannot be represented by SVG groups."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/capture/script/index.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 1481,
                  "endLine": 1500,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "  // A planar quad is affine exactly when q2 = q1 + q3 - q0. Promote every\n  // non-affine plane to the outermost containing 3D context so capture stamps\n  // the composited context once, while affine matrix3d cases stay vectorized.\n  const _nonAffineProjectiveRoots = new Set();\n  for (const _pel of _projectiveInfluenced) {\n    const _style = getComputedStyle(_pel);\n    if (_style.perspective != null && _style.perspective !== '' && _style.perspective !== 'none') {\n      let _root = _pel;\n      while (_root.parentElement != null && _projectiveInfluenced.has(_root.parentElement)) _root = _root.parentElement;\n      _nonAffineProjectiveRoots.add(_root);\n    }\n    const _q = _projectedQuads.get(_pel);\n    if (_q == null) continue;\n    const _rx = _q[2].x - (_q[1].x + _q[3].x - _q[0].x);\n    const _ry = _q[2].y - (_q[1].y + _q[3].y - _q[0].y);\n    if (Math.hypot(_rx, _ry) <= 0.02) continue;\n    let _root = _pel;\n    while (_root.parentElement != null && _projectiveInfluenced.has(_root.parentElement)) _root = _root.parentElement;\n    _nonAffineProjectiveRoots.add(_root);\n  }"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
